Replace the vendor Mali-400 driver (ARM r6p0, user API 800) with ARM's GPL
Utgard r6p2-01rel0 kernel driver (API 900), which matches the public Linux
fbdev/X11 Mali userspace (r6p2). Apply with -p1 inside drivers/gpu/mali400
after extracting DX910-SW-99002-r6p2-01rel0.tgz there (kernel/build.sh).

- Kbuild/Kconfig: vendor in-tree build glue (MALI_PLATFORM_SC8830, DT).
- platform/sc8830: unchanged vendor clock/power/DFS code.
- mali_kernel_linux.c: DFS module params, power-mode hooks for the platform.
- mali_mem_validation.c: accept exactly the fb0 range (sprdfb probes after
  Mali), instead of the vendor's 'accept any physical range'.

